prompt.text:
Repair the CommonJS module below. It must export exactly `{ dispatchMessage }`.

`dispatchMessage(handlers, message)` processes handlers sequentially. `handlers` must be an array containing only functions; otherwise throw `TypeError` before invoking any handler. Each handler receives `message` and may return a value or a promise. Await each result before calling the next handler. Return a promise resolving to the first result that is not `undefined`; if every result is `undefined`, resolve to `undefined`. If a handler throws or rejects, stop and reject with the same error. The handlers array must not be mutated.

The current implementation fails to await handler results, so a promise resolving to `undefined` is mistaken for a handled result and later handlers are skipped. Return a corrected complete source file.

```javascript
'use strict';

async function dispatchMessage(handlers, message) {
  if (!Array.isArray(handlers) || handlers.some((handler) => typeof handler !== 'function')) {
    throw new TypeError('handlers must be functions');
  }
  for (const handler of handlers) {
    const result = handler(message);
    if (result !== undefined) return result;
  }
  return undefined;
}

module.exports = { dispatchMessage };
```

